# JPWB TypeScript Codebase Semantic Analysis and Assurance Corpus

## Proposed corpus charter, manifest, and W0-17 candidate

**Document ID:** `JAN-CSAA-000`

**Canonical title:** JPWB TypeScript Codebase Semantic Analysis and Assurance Corpus

**Version:** `0.2.1`

**Status:** Proposed

**Settledness:** HYPOTHESIS candidate; artifact standing not conferred

**Classification:** Program working-reference candidate under the Stage A preparation grant

**Governing status:** `REG-D-017` establishes the CSAA program and permanent identifier reservations; this Proposed member is not adopted and does not govern

**Role:** Proposed corpus entry point, scope and authority-boundary charter, controlled manifest, and staged authoring-commission candidate

**Authority:** None as a CSAA member. `REG-D-017` authorizes preparation, ledger/review work, and a W0-17 adoption package only

**Stage A grant:** `JPWB-REG-005 REG-D-017` — EFFECTIVE; Draft ledger and self-review are closed, while append-only carriage confirmation remains pending

**Stage B gate:** W0-17 not presented; exact-version/digest adoption and Wave 1 activation remain pending

**Scope:** Semantic analysis and conventional software assurance of the manifest-resolved TypeScript, JavaScript, and TypeScript-bearing Svelte implementation in `JanumiCode/janumiprofessionalworkbench`

**Applicability:** This charter candidate and, only after their own commissions and adoptions, the controlled `JAN-CSAA-001` through `JAN-CSAA-011` members and their allocated reference artifacts

**Governs:** If and only if W0-17 later adopts the exact version and digest, the CSAA program boundary, source-of-truth model, semantic baselines, manifest, document responsibilities, staged commissions, and closure rules within the granted scope

**Does not govern:** Canon meaning, professional-work semantics, infrastructure assurance, Janumi product standing, exact executable shapes owned by repository reference artifacts, provider selection, procurement, implementation permission, oracle changes, or any uncommissioned later-wave work

**Parent and inherited authorities:** `JPWB-CON-000`, `JPWB-DOC-001`, `JPWB-DOC-002`, `JPWB-DOC-003`, `JPWB-DOC-004`, and the applicable `JPWB-REG-005` entries, each only for its owned concern

**Precedence and conflict routing:** Canon and recognized enforced reference artifacts retain their concern ownership. Apparent conflict, missing authority, or incompatible meaning SHALL be recorded and routed to `JPWB-REG-005`; this charter SHALL NOT silently reconcile it

**Requirement ledger:** [JAN-CSAA-000 Requirement Ledger](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Requirement Ledger.md>)

**Verification owner:** The author owns extraction and self-review evidence; an independent reviewer owns the Proposed-candidate adversarial review; neither may confer Normative status

**Change authority and procedure:** Authors MAY revise Draft text under `REG-D-017`. Draft SHALL advance to Proposed only after ledger closure and self-review. Material Proposed-byte changes SHALL receive affected re-review; Normative status or material Normative change SHALL require an exact-version/digest sponsor act in `JPWB-REG-005`

**Review and evidence companions:** [Preparation Evidence Snapshot](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Preparation Evidence Snapshot.md>); [Self-Review](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Self Review.md>); [Draft-to-Proposed Promotion Record](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Draft-to-Proposed Promotion Record.md>); [Independent Review](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Independent Review.md>); [Integrity Manifest](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - Integrity Manifest.md>); [W0-17 Adoption Instrument](<records/JAN-CSAA-000 - W0-17 Adoption Instrument.md>)

**Companion enforced artifacts:** None at this pre-executable charter stage; see §§9.4, 14, and 18–21 for future commission, authority, and conformance controls

**Conformance-test references:** None currently govern this charter; `JAN-CSAA-006` through `JAN-CSAA-008` are reserved but unauthored and uncommissioned

**Audience:** Coding agents, software architects, implementers, assurance engineers, security reviewers, tool integrators, and maintainers

**Background input:** [Initial Chat](<Initial Chat.md>)

**Structural exemplar:** [Recursive Professional Harness document-set README](<../Recursive Professional Harness/README.md>)

**Supersedes:** None

**Superseded by:** None

**Normative keywords:** SHALL, SHALL NOT, SHOULD, SHOULD NOT, MAY

---

## 1. Proposal in one sentence

Create a controlled, RPH-shaped documentation corpus that specifies how the JPWB TypeScript repository is represented, analyzed, queried, assured, exposed to coding agents, implemented with qualified analysis providers, and verified against independent executable oracles.

The corpus is deliberately limited to conventional software-engineering assurance of the codebase. It does not define infrastructure assurance, professional-work semantics, or intent-to-implementation traceability.

---

## 2. Stage A disposition and remaining decision

`JPWB-REG-005 REG-D-017` records the sponsor's separate **RATIFY** disposition of W0-01 through W0-16. It establishes **Codebase Semantic Analysis and Assurance** (`JAN-CSAA`) as a bounded program working-reference series and permanently reserves `JAN-CSAA-000` through `JAN-CSAA-011`. Reservation does not confer member authority.

Stage A records:

1. the working name, non-product standing, program authority form, scope, and first subject;
2. the dirty-worktree evidence and read-only execution boundary;
3. the permanent prefix, identifiers, lifecycle, and document-control rules;
4. the provider-independent semantic baselines in W0-09 through W0-14;
5. the concrete provider, architecture, persistence, gate, licensing, deployment, and topology deferrals in W0-15;
6. the per-member review, oracle, and `JPWB-REG-005` adoption procedure in W0-16;
7. approval in principle of the W0-08 documentation-only commission for `JAN-CSAA-001`, `JAN-CSAA-002`, and `JAN-CSAA-005`.

