## 3. Current governance posture

### 3.1 Stage A does not confer member authority

The operative [JPWB Constitution](<../canon/JPWB-CON-000 Constitution.md>) defines a closed rule of recognition:

- the six named canon artifacts govern their owned concerns;
- individually ratified `JPWB-SPEC-nnn` deep reference specifications may govern a subsystem at `HYPOTHESIS` settledness;
- program working references govern only when an explicit registered sponsor grant names their scope and standing;
- enforced repository reference artifacts own exact executable shapes;
- unrecognized prose does not govern, regardless of title or deontic voice.

Accordingly:

- `REG-D-017` is the effective registered sponsor grant for the bounded CSAA program;
- `JAN-CSAA-000@0.2.1` retains only its recorded pre-adoption lifecycle status and remains an unadopted candidate;
- `JAN-CSAA-000` through `JAN-CSAA-011` are permanent, non-reusable reservations;
- only `JAN-CSAA-000` is authored;
- W0-08 is approved in principle but inactive until W0-17;
- no proposed requirement is binding until the resulting artifact receives its required governance status;
- a future `JPWB-SPEC-nnn` successor SHALL receive the identifier allocated through the canon process and SHALL record its relationship to this proposal rather than silently changing this proposal's recorded ID.

### 3.2 Relationship to existing authorities

This corpus SHALL specialize, not duplicate or amend, the existing authority stack:

| Concern | Existing owner | CSAA relationship |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First principles and rule of recognition | `JPWB-CON-000` | Inherited without restatement or weakening |
| Reasoning, judgment, operation, and concept of employment | `JPWB-DOC-001` | Specialized only for code-analysis employment |
| Canonical Janumi vocabulary | `JPWB-DOC-002` | Reused; CSAA terms SHALL remain software-analysis terms |
| JPWB semantic objects and invariants | `JPWB-DOC-003` | Not redefined; CSAA may evaluate code against separately supplied executable software constraints but does not interpret professional semantics |
| Coding-agent conduct and process | `JPWB-DOC-004` | `JAN-CSAA-010` becomes a scoped analysis profile, not a replacement protocol |
| Open decisions and divergence | `JPWB-REG-005` | Used for commissions, rulings, and unresolved semantic conflicts |
| Engineering practice | Operative `JPWB-DOC-004`, especially Section 7 | Specialized with code-analysis mechanics but not weakened or duplicated |
| Exact repository shapes | Enforced schemas, generated contracts, migrations, and conformance tests | Read and checked; never redefined by an analyzer |
| Existing implementation behavior | Source code and observed executions | The factual subject being analyzed, not self-certifying authority over intended meaning |

The [JPWB Agent Operating Protocol](<../canon/JPWB-DOC-004 Agent Operating Protocol.md>) is the operative owner of agent procedure and engineering practice. The [standalone Engineering Constitution](<../Recursive Professional Harness/Janumi Professional Workbench - Engineering Constitution.md>) and the RPH README remain useful structural and historical inputs, but they are outside the live rule of recognition and SHALL NOT be cited as current governing authority. Any durable content reused from them SHALL receive a governed transplant into a recognized artifact; historical material is not reactivated by reference.

### 3.3 Staged authority-transfer lifecycle

The intended paths follow `JPWB-CON-000 B6` and `JPWB-REG-005 REG-D-009`.

For a program working corpus:

```text
Draft charter proposal
    ↓ REG-D-017 Stage A program grant and preparation commission
Draft exact charter + closed ledger + self-review
    ↓ author advances the reviewed candidate to Proposed
Proposed exact-version/digest charter + independent review
    ↓ separate W0-17 sponsor conferral in JPWB-REG-005
Normative HYPOTHESIS-grade JAN-CSAA-000 + active W0-08 Wave 1 commission
    ↓ later per-member conferrals and executable discharge
Enforced schemas, types, rules, fixtures, and conformance tests
    ↓ recorded program completion, supersession, or retirement
Durable obligations remain in enforced repository artifacts
```

For a canon deep reference specification:

```text
Specification commission
    ↓ authoring only; no authority conferred
Draft JPWB-SPEC-nnn
    ↓ individual ratification in JPWB-REG-005
HYPOTHESIS-grade subsystem specification
    ↓ fully performed by enforced artifacts and conformance tests
Recorded sponsor act transfers authority under B6
    ↓
Specification retires; executable obligation surface remains
```

The corpus SHALL be written for eventual discharge into enforced artifacts, not for permanent prose accretion.

